Rule 1 (integer dim must be within valid range)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1) ∧ (v_2 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1)) ∧ (v_2 < ndim(v_1))
>>
Rule 2 (tuple dims must each be within valid range and count not exceed rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= (v_2.len ≥ 1) ∧ (v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : (v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1))
>>
Rule 4 (integer dim: negative dims are allowed only within rank; non-negative must be less than rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 < 0 then (0 - v_2) ≤ ndim(v_1) else v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (tuple dims: each negative dim is allowed only within rank; non-negative must be less than rank)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= (v_2.len ≥ 1 ∧ v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : if v_2[i] < 0 then (0 - v_2[i]) ≤ ndim(v_1) else v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
